discussion_comments.comment_body:
**[Suggestion]** `findMetaTrigger` filters issue events only by the upper bound (`created_at > maxUpdatedAt`) but omits the lower-bound `windowSince` filter that `fetchNewComments` (line 645) correctly applies. — Failure scenario: bot is assigned to issue X; event dispatched and key recorded in `dispatchedEvents`. After 500+ other events evict the key from the cursor trim, a sticky `assign` notification re-appears with bumped `updated_at`. `findMetaTrigger` re-fetches the event pages; the old event satisfies `created_at <= maxUpdatedAt` and is no longer in the dedup list, so it is returned as a fresh trigger. The adapter dispatches the same assignment body a second time, presenting a stale action as if it just happened.

```suggestion
    const event = events.findLast((candidate) => {
      if (
        !candidate.created_at ||
        candidate.created_at > ctx.maxUpdatedAt ||
        candidate.created_at <= ctx.windowSince
      ) {
        return false;
      }
```

<details><summary>中文说明</summary>

`findMetaTrigger` 仅按上界（`created_at > maxUpdatedAt`）过滤 issue event，缺少 `fetchNewComments`（第 645 行）正确使用的下界 `windowSince` 过滤。当 `dispatchedEvents` 被裁剪超过 MAX_DISPATCHED（500）后，过时的 `review_requested` 或 `assign` 事件可能被重新选中并重复下发。修复：在 `findLast` 谓词中添加 `candidate.created_at <= ctx.windowSince` 下界检查。

</details>

_— qwen3.7-max via Qwen Code /review_

