**[Critical]** `processMetaLane` does not check `dispatchedBodies` before dispatching the PR/issue body — Failure scenario: a `mention` notification and a `review_requested`/`assign` notification for the same thread arrive in the same poll batch. The mention enters `processPerCommentLane` → `tryFirstContactBody` dispatches the PR body and records `dispatchedBodies`. Then `review_requested` enters `processMetaLane` which never consults `dispatchedBodies` — it dispatches the same body again with a different messageId (`pull-body-99` vs `issue-body-99`). The agent receives duplicate content.

```suggestion
  private async processMetaLane(
    ctx: LaneContext,
    kind: 'pull' | 'issue',
    trigger: { actor: string; key: string },
    framing: string,
  ): Promise<void> {
    const { chatId, threadId, issueNumber, subjectTitle } = ctx;
    const bodyKey = `${chatId}|${threadId}`;
    if (this.cursor.dispatchedBodies?.includes(bodyKey)) {
      this.recordDispatched('dispatchedEvents', [trigger.key]);
      return;
    }
```

<details><summary>中文说明</summary>

`processMetaLane` 在下发 PR/issue body 前没有检查 `dispatchedBodies`。当同一线程的 `mention` 和 `review_requested`/`assign` 通知在同一轮轮询中到达时，mention 路径通过 `tryFirstContactBody` 下发 body 并记录 `dispatchedBodies`，而 meta lane 不检查该集合，会以不同 messageId 再次下发相同内容，导致 agent 收到重复信息。

</details>

_— qwen3.7-max via Qwen Code /review_

